Z||000006||1FST2M6||02-23-2001||08:10 AM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> nice job!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> thats awsome! got pics? or a scan of the time slip? where are you located? is there a dyno near you? <A HREF="http://www.dynojet.com" TARGET=_blank>www.dynojet.com</A>   the nitrous works kit whats the part #  13093? <P>the car does run under positive pressure when the nitrous is on.. but unless he has the proper fuel and timing mapping on the e-prom or a boost sensative fuel pressure unit he won't realize enough gain to justify the cost of the sensor (about $80 new from NAPA) in addition to the e-prom having to be switched cause it'll run like crap off the bottle. my car did. we found a good happy median and i and GT Bastard are happy with it's mapping.  <P>have you thought about running a nitrous retard switch? MSD make an adjustable retard box for about $80 from 1-10*.  <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 02-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||v6freak79||02-23-2001||09:49 AM||||i'm in memphis, i work at lucky motor sports, and yes i have axcess to a dyno, 205hp off gas, 292hp on gas...the map sensor, just kinda fools the little air sensor in the throttle body, without it, it kinda falls on it's face. don't ask, i don't know, we just had it on the dyno and were tryin stuff, and it added 7hp on the gas, i'm thinking it because when i spray there is such a great change in vacume pressure or something, but it helped ....14.0/ at98mph off gas. there should be more of a drop, but i tend to have traction problems....||||reg||1
Z||000008||1FST2M6||02-23-2001||10:06 AM||||you having wheel hop problems? i did.. i've got video of mine shakin/bouncing through 330' mark! i never was able to figure out how to stop that.. the map sensor reading positive on the gas ups the fuel injector pulse width. giving you more fuel.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> a Stillen FPR would help even more... they are vacuum sensative and for every .5psi over vacuum your fuel pressure is uped 2+psi. every little bit helps. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6dyno.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6dyno.jpg</A>   my tiny 40shot..    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <P>what engine mods do you have now? what clutch are you running the DF or the gold? I fried my CF-DF and they refunded my $. can you scan your dyno sheet and post it?<P>not a real decent depiction but still fun to look at... over 300hp and 350lbft at the shift..   <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6allgear.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6allgear.jpg</A> <P><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg">    <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 02-23-2001).]||||reg||1
